# Start-up (spec M9-4): the welcome, the tip of the day and the start-up notices.

menu-help-tip = Tip of the day

start-welcome-title = Welcome to MyChess
start-welcome-intro = MyChess keeps your files in one folder that you can see and use. Pick the language of the interface below; you can change it later in the View menu.
start-welcome-language = Language
start-welcome-folder = Your MyChess folder: { $path }
start-welcome-subfolders = Engine holds chess engines, Databases holds your game collections and Books holds opening books. Nothing in it is ever deleted or overwritten by the program.
start-welcome-preparing = Preparing the folder...
start-welcome-no-folder = The program could not find your home folder, so the MyChess folder was not created. Everything else works.
start-welcome-problem-file = A file is in the way, so this folder was not created: { $path }
start-welcome-problem-create = This folder could not be created: { $path }
start-welcome-engine-found = Engine found in the Engine folder: { $name }. It will be added to your list of engines.
start-welcome-engine-none = No engine in the Engine folder yet. Put an engine program there, or add one in Tools > Engines.
start-welcome-portable = Portable mode: the preferences and the data stay next to the program.
start-welcome-go = Get started

start-show-tip = Show a tip when MyChess starts
start-tip-title = Tip of the day
start-tip-number = Tip { $number } of { $total }
start-tip-previous = Previous
start-tip-next = Next
start-tip-close = Close

start-notice-portable-not-writable = Portable mode is off: the folder next to the program cannot be written ({ $path }).
start-notice-portable-unavailable = Portable mode is off: the folder of the program is unknown.
start-notice-no-home = The home folder is unknown: the MyChess folder was not created.
start-notice-folder-problem = The MyChess folder could not be prepared: { $path }

tip-1 = Press F1 at any time to open the manual at the chapter that matches what you are doing.
tip-2 = Drag a game from the game list onto the tab of another database to copy it there.
tip-3 = Ctrl+Tab (Cmd+Tab on macOS) goes to the next open database. Up to eight databases and the Clipbase can be open at once.
tip-4 = The Clipbase is a scratch database that is always open. Use Edit > Copy game to Clipbase to collect games from several databases in one place.
tip-5 = The space bar turns the analysis of the main engine on and off, and F2, F3 and F4 start the engines assigned to those keys.
tip-6 = Tools > Engines adds UCI and XBoard engines, looks for the ones installed on your computer and imports the engines.dat file of the Scid.
tip-7 = Open the Opening tree panel from View > Panes to see how the games of your database continue from the current position, and the Opening books panel for Polyglot books.
tip-8 = Play > New Chess960 game starts from any of the 960 starting positions, numbered 0 to 959. Number 518 is the usual one.
tip-9 = View > Theme opens a window where you choose the theme, the board, the pieces and the accent color, with a live preview.
tip-10 = Ctrl+F (Cmd+F on macOS) turns the board around.
